Hi Wojciech,

The notation is [condition #, choice #], so the results that you are reporting are interesting...

I have run parameter recovery with the LBA model, and it recovers drift rates just fine—are you simulating data using the LBA model or are you using another method?

The d parameter is indeed equivalent to k. I am sorry for the confusion; I cannot remember why we decided to change that at the moment, but it may be worth renaming that variable to k.

What are the differences like? We are using the same estimation procedures (including priors).

Best,

Nate
